From: PANVK G57 / Helio G99 JM port
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/v9: program Shader Environment FAU count from shader metadata

Root cause of the "clear-only" v9 graphics result.

On Valhall v9 the Shader Environment descriptor carries BOTH the FAU
pointer and an FAU *count*. The port previously programmed only
`cfg.fau` (the pointer) and left `fau_count` at 0. With a zero count the
hardware uploads no fast-access uniforms, so the vertex shader receives
no viewport/position uniforms and the fragment shader receives no blend
descriptor pointer. The job chain still completes (exception_status 0x01
DONE on both MALLOC_VERTEX and FRAGMENT) but nothing is rasterized.

Counts MUST come from the compiled shader metadata (`fau.total_count`).
They are not architectural constants: the captured 64x64 triangle
workload reports VS count=4 and FS count=3, so hardcoding either value
would break any other shader.

A/B evidence (identical binary except these two lines):
  A (fau_count absent) : 0 / 4096 non-black  -> CLEAR-ONLY
  B (fau_count present): 4096 / 4096 non-black, all 255,0,0,255
Repeated as ab_A2 (0/4096) and b_final (4096/4096).

--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -2298,6 +2298,7 @@
                    : panvk_priv_mem_dev_addr(vs->spds.pos_triangles);
       cfg.thread_storage = draw->tls;
       cfg.fau = cmdbuf->state.gfx.vs.push_uniforms;
+      cfg.fau_count = vs->fau.total_count;
    }
 }
 
@@ -2529,6 +2530,8 @@
          panvk_shader_only_variant(get_fs(cmdbuf))->spd);
       cfg.shader.thread_storage = draw->tls;
       cfg.shader.fau = cmdbuf->state.gfx.fs.push_uniforms;
+      cfg.shader.fau_count =
+         panvk_shader_only_variant(get_fs(cmdbuf))->fau.total_count;
    }
 
    return VK_SUCCESS;
